{"name":"Goody Two Shoes","hex":"#c2ba8e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goody two shoes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A goody-goody; a person who is almost always perfectly well-behaved, with an implication of smugness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goody_two_shoes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goody Two Shoes (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Goody Two Shoes\" is the debut solo single by Adam Ant, released on 7 May 1982. It became Ant's third overall number one in the UK and his highest-charting song in the US, where it peaked at number 12. The song's lyrics are satirical, mocking the UK tabloid press and their obsession with Ant's clean lifestyle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goody_Two_Shoes_(song)","wikidata":"Q5583747"},{"title":"The History of Little Goody Two-Shoes","blocks":[{"text":"The History of Little Goody Two-Shoes is a children's story published by John Newbery in London in 1765. The author of the book remains unclear, but Oliver Goldsmith is generally considered the most likely. The story popularized the phrase \"goody two-shoes\" as a descriptor for an excessively virtuous person or do-gooder. Historian V. M. Braganza refers to it as one of the first works of children's literature, perhaps the earliest children's novel in English. It was highly influential to subsequent authors, revolutionary in the development of its literary genre, and popular, noted for its female heroine in a realist setting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg/330px-Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_History_of_Little_Goody_Two-Shoes","wikidata":"Q12060236"},{"title":"Two Shoes","blocks":[{"text":"Two Shoes is the second studio album by Australian ska-jazz band the Cat Empire, which was issued on 19 April 2005. It is the follow-up to their successful self-titled debut album. It was recorded in November to December 2004 in Havana, Cuba. It débuted at the top of the ARIA Albums Chart and is the band's first number 1 album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Two_Shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Shoes","wikidata":"Q4171750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg/250px-Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg/250px-Goody_Two_Shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoody_Two_Shoes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg/500px-Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg/500px-Goody_Two-Shoes_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoody_Two-Shoes_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/GTShoesWoodcut.jpg/250px-GTShoesWoodcut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1